// Package gen provides deterministic data-generation primitives for stroppy
// workloads.
//
// A value generated by this package is a pure function of a root seed, a
// semantic domain name, a field name, an entity index, and (for values that
// need more than one 64-bit word) a sub-draw index. There is no mutable
// per-draw state and no shared global PRNG: any entity of any field is
// reachable in O(1) without affecting any other entity.
//
// # Coordinates
//
// The derivation hierarchy is:
//
//	Root   = New(seed)
//	Domain = root.Domain("tpcc/item@1")   // workload-owned, versioned name
//	Field  = domain.Field("i_im_id")      // one logical column's stream
//	Draw   = field.At(entityIndex)        // cursor for one entity's draws
//
// Domain names are chosen by the workload and carry an explicit version
// suffix (the "@1" above). Renaming or renumbering a domain changes the data;
// inserting an unrelated domain does not. Field names partition one domain's
// stream so editing one field never shifts another field's sequence.
//
// Worker identity, chunk boundaries, batch sizes, and the executor step name
// never enter the coordinate. A dataset generated with workers=N is therefore
// byte-identical to the same dataset generated with workers=1, and resuming a
// load at entity E produces the same suffix as a full run from entity E.
//
// # Seeds
//
// A seed of 0 is a valid, deterministic seed. Operators wanting a
// non-deterministic run pass a random seed explicitly; the package never
// silently substitutes one.
//
// # Allocation
//
// Preparation (constructing Root, Domain, Field, and prepared batches and
// tables) may allocate. Generating a value at a coordinate — scalar draws,
// alphabet fills, weighted picks over prepared tables — allocates nothing on
// the hot path.
package gen
